  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"terminal#17246\"], \"answer\": \"This looks like the crash reported in terminal#17246. Merging a tab into another window crashes WindowsTerminal.exe with 0xc0000005 in Microsoft.Terminal.Control.dll, and every window dies because they share one process. In that ticket, a maintainer-side analysis found that when a tab is torn off or closed, XAML calls OnCreateAutomationPeer on a TermControl that is detached and has no _interactivity. That causes a null-pointer dereference. The ticket also shows a second access violation inside Windows.UI.Xaml (DXamlCore::EnsureDragDrop). The archive doesn't show a confirmed fix. Your report suggests the problem still happens on 1.24.2605.12001 even though #17246 is closed. I'd suggest three things. (1) Add your event-log signature (fault offset 0x2c924, 1.24.2605.12001) to #17246, or open a new issue that links it, and say that it reproduces on 1.24. (2) Until it's fixed, avoid drag-merging tabs between windows. Use the move-tab or move-pane actions, or keep the work in one window. (3) Keep the crash dump and share it through a private channel with the maintainers, since it contains scrollback. The RADAR_PRE_LEAK warning and the large scrollback buffers aren't mentioned in #17246, so note them as extra detail.\"}",
